Flashing factory image using Netgear UI and subsequently rebooting may result in bricking the router as reported for **very similar WNDR4500v3**.  The solution is to flash factory image using Netgear UI and immediately flash sysupgrade image via SSH.
[[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/solved-netgear-wndr4500v3-brick-bootloop-after-first-reboot/111333|See WNDR4500v3 Unbrick & Install thread]]


**UNVERIFIED FOR WNDR4300v2 as of 7 Feb 2022**
Summarised instructions, based on WNDR4500v3, to apply both the factory and sysupgrade images is as follows:

  - Use the Netgear UI and flash the squashfs-**factory**.img to the router.  The router will automatically restart when the install is complete.
  - Next, SSH into the router at 192.168.1.1 and execute the following commands to install the 21.02.1 squashfs-**sysupgrade** image release in this example:
<code>
          cd /tmp
          
          wget https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/21.02.1/targets/ath79/nand/openwrt-21.02.1-ath79-nand-netgear_wndr4300-v2-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
          
          sysupgrade -v /tmp/openwrt-21.02.1-ath79-nand-netgear_wndr4300-v2-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
</code>
  - You will be disconnected.  The router will eventually restart and OpenWrt is ready for use.  The router should no longer brick itself when powered off.
==== OEM easy installation ====
This is for installing for the first time OpenWrt on the router (still with the stock firmware): This method was tested by one user and reported here [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/netgear-4300-for-openwrt-in-2022/127605/23|See Netgear 4300 for OpenWrt in 2022]]
  - Connect your computer to the router with an ethernet cable and browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1/%%''\\ (default credentials are ''admin password'')
  - In Netgear web interface go to:\\ ''<color purple>Advanced > Administration > Firmware Upgrade </color>''
  - Download both factory and sysupgrade files from either the 
    * **Firmware selector tool** https://firmware-selector.openwrt.org/?version=21.02.3&target=ath79%2Fnand&id=netgear_wndr4300-v2 
    * or 
    * **Release page** https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/21.02.3/targets/ath79/nand/. 
  - Upload the Openwrt firmware: //openwrt-21.02.3-ath79-nand-netgear_wndr4300-v2-**squashfs-factory.img**//
  - Proceed with the firmware installation and wait some minutes until it finish.
  - Once Openwrt, has been flashed. Navigate to <color purple>//''%%http://192.168.1.1/%%''//</color> and set a password for the Openwrt.
  - Navigate to <color #00a2e8>System -- Backup/Flash Firmware</color> and upload the lastest (in this case 21.02.3) //openwrt-21.02.3-ath79-nand-netgear_wndr4300-v2-**squashfs-sysupgrade.bin**// in //Flash new firmware image//. Let it upgrade and reboot. 
  - Now you can enjoy the latest Openwrt on Netgear 4300V2, without even using SSH or telnet access. 

